 - **No test framework found** — skip regression check, reviewer verdict still runs
 - **Lint tools not installed** — skip that check silently, don't fail
 - **Auto-fix introduces new issues** — counts as a new failure, cycle continues
+- **Baseline detection wrong** — if `git stash` fails (no local changes), skip baseline; running tests on the working tree IS the baseline
+- **Subagent timeout on large diffs** — if the reviewer subagent times out, split the diff into smaller chunks and review each separately
+- **Secrets in test fixtures** — static scan will flag hardcoded strings in test files; these are usually false positives. Note them explicitly in the fix prompt if intentional
+- **Cross-language projects** — run the appropriate linter for EACH language in the repo; don't assume Python just because the main app is Python
